<title>USA: U.S. Q2 revised corporate profits fell 0.2 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Q2 revised corporate profits fell 0.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerce Department revised estimates of second quarter profits by U.S. corporations, with comparisons. Profits before tax include inventory valuation and capital consumption adjustments.</p>
<p>Data are chain weighted and expressed in seasonally adjusted annual rates of billions of dollars, with second quarter percent changes from the first quarter.</p>
<p> -		  Pct--Q2'96--Prev.----Q1'96----1995</p>
<p> -  After Tax  -0.2  408.1  407.4    408.8   380.2</p>
<p> -  Before Tax  1.7  655.8  653.8    645.1   586.6</p>
<p> Tax Liability  1.3  236.4  236.7    233.4   218.7</p>
<p>The department said the after-tax decline in corporate profits in the second quarter was the first drop since a 2.0 percent decrease in the second quarter of 1995.</p>
</text>
